  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Box command (code 7). Shows the label BOX. The first press sets a corner, the second press sets the other corner. Then the box moves with the cursor until the third press. Then fill_box fills the box in current_colour."},
    {"at":55,"placement":"line","text":"Frame command (code 4). Shows the label FRAME. The first press sets a corner, the second press sets the other corner. Then the frame moves with the cursor until the third press. Then brush_rect draws the frame with the brush in current_colour."},
    {"at":110,"placement":"line","text":"Moves the corner (shape_x1, shape_y1) with the cursor and shows the rectangle with XOR (xor_rect) until a new button press. Then erases the rectangle. A long press off the pad erases it, restores current_colour from saved_colour and goes to tool_exit. Box, Frame and Copy use it."},
    {"at":167,"placement":"line","text":"Moves the rectangle with the cursor until a new button press. The cursor sets the corner (shape_x1, shape_y1). The corner (shape_x0, shape_y0) keeps its distance delta_x/delta_y, in the limits 0-max_x and 0-max_y. Shows the rectangle with XOR and erases it at the end. A long press off the pad goes to tool_exit."},
    {"at":167,"placement":"side","text":"delta_x = shape_x0 - shape_x1 (16 bits)."},
    {"at":326,"placement":"side","text":"High byte not 0: shape_x0 is max_x."},
    {"at":380,"placement":"line","text":"Fills the rectangle with the corners (shape_x0, shape_y0) and (shape_x1, shape_y1) in current_colour: draws one horizontal line ($2788) for each row, with the one-pixel brush at $1868. Puts the smaller coordinates in shape_x0/shape_y0. Restores brush_ptr at the end."},
    {"at":383,"placement":"side","text":"brush_ptr = $1868: the brush of one pixel."},
    {"at":455,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the rectangle with the corners (shape_x0, shape_y0) and (shape_x1, shape_y1) with XOR: plot_vector = $18c2, then draw_rect. A second call erases it."},
    {"at":463,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the rectangle with the corners (shape_x0, shape_y0) and (shape_x1, shape_y1) through plot_vector ($279e). When the corners are in one column or one row, draws one line. Else draws four lines: left side, bottom, right side, top. The 2nd, 3rd and 4th line start one pixel after their corner."},
    {"at":597,"placement":"line","text":"Draws the rectangle with the corners (shape_x0, shape_y0) and (shape_x1, shape_y1) with the brush: plot_vector = plot_brush, then draw_rect."}
  ],
